      "attributes": [
        {
          "doc_text": " Creates an iterator which, starting from an initial item,",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            49,
            110
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " computes each successive item from the preceding one.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            111,
            168
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            169,
            172
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " This iterator stores an optional item (`Option<T>`) and a successor closure (`impl FnMut(&T) -> Option<T>`).",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            173,
            285
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " Its `next` method returns the stored optional item and",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            286,
            344
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " if it is `Some(val)` calls the stored closure on `&val` to compute and store its successor.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            345,
            440
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " The iterator will apply the closure successively to the stored option's value until the option is `None`.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            441,
            550
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " This also means that once the stored option is `None` it will remain `None`,",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            551,
            631
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " as the closure will not be called again, so the created iterator is a [`FusedIterator`].",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            632,
            724
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " The iterator's items will be the initial item and all of its successors as calculated by the successor closure.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            725,
            840
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            841,
            844
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " ```",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            845,
            852
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " use std::iter::successors;",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            853,
            883
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            884,
            887
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " let powers_of_10 = successors(Some(1_u16), |n| n.checked_mul(10));",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            888,
            958
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " assert_eq!(powers_of_10.collect::<Vec<_>>(), &[1, 10, 100, 1_000, 10_000]);",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            959,
            1038
          ],
